From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: bonsai-27b-fusion <noreply@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Thu, 1 Jan 2026 00:00:00 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] docs(fusion): the four Bonsai packs, measured properly

Replaces the earlier smoke test (43.7-44.2 t/s, no quality numbers) with the full suite
on this tree's build: llama-bench f16 and turbo3, PPL on wikitext-2 in both KV types,
and greedy coherence, with a 50 C thermal gate before every task.

Throughput is identical across the four (0.2-0.5 percent spread), turbo3 KV costs the
same 4-6 percent of generation everywhere, and quality differs by 13 percent in PPL -
but these are not the same weights (heretic is a fine-tune, derisked and crack are
modified), so that spread is about the weights, not the packing.

The coherence column needed a correction: the suite ran -n 32, which cut every model off
mid-reasoning, so the arithmetic check recorded an intermediate step rather than the
answer. Re-run with -n 400: all four reach 391 and all four write a working
reverse-string one-liner.
